  era: "c. 1695\u20131763 \xB7 Section 17 \xB7 Regional Powers \xB7 18th century"
  title: Jats
  text: The Jats, peasant-warriors of the region around Delhi and Agra, built a powerful state under Churaman and Badan Singh. It peaked under Suraj Mal, who died in 1763 and built the fort-palaces of Bharatpur and Deeg.
